load ../infoflow-input-provenance.maude

--- Input-side provenance narrowing at a marked crossing. Coverage searches show
--- the carried set never under-reports (a reaching or fallback-widened source
--- still denies); bite searches show the refinement is real (a source with no
--- path into the coercion's arguments needs no grant, and literal-only
--- arguments carry nothing).

--- ============================ COVERAGE, leak reachable =====================

--- Coverage: a confidential source attributed into the coercion's arguments and
--- NOT granted denies the crossing. Narrowing never waives a reaching source.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE :
  src(sA, hi, false) src(sB, lo, false) crossing(rs(sA) . nilR)
  =>* C:Cfg leak .

--- Coverage: an UNATTRIBUTABLE root widens the carried set to every source --
--- the fail-closed fallback. sB never appears in the roots, yet its
--- confidential, ungranted read still denies (pre-narrowing behavior exactly).
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE :
  src(sA, hi, true) src(sB, hi, false) crossing(rs(sA) . unknown . nilR)
  =>* C:Cfg leak .

--- Coverage: a grant on the wrong source does not cover a reaching one -- the
--- carried source itself must carry the grant flag.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE :
  src(sA, hi, false) src(sB, lo, true) crossing(rs(sA) . nilR)
  =>* C:Cfg leak .

--- ============================ BITE, no leak ================================

--- Bite: the headline narrowing. sB is confidential and UNGRANTED but has no
--- path into the coercion's arguments (all roots attributed, none to sB), so
--- the crossing needs no sB grant. sA reaches and is granted.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE :
  src(sA, hi, true) src(sB, hi, false) crossing(rs(sA) . nilR)
  =>* RESIDUAL:Cfg leak .

--- Bite: a reaching, granted source arms cleanly -- no denial.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE :
  src(sA, hi, true) src(sB, lo, false) crossing(rs(sA) . nilR)
  =>* RESIDUAL:Cfg leak .

--- Bite: literal-only arguments (no roots) carry no source at all -- a
--- constant release denies nothing, whatever the rule read.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE :
  src(sA, hi, false) src(sB, hi, false) crossing(nilR)
  =>* RESIDUAL:Cfg leak .
